## MMU-gather and destination-page observations

Each sidecar contains one gather setup with all four recorded phases (`setup`, `initial`, `actual_post`, `returned`) captured, no omitted setups, and no omitted unpaired events. The aggregate gather status is `incomplete` because each capture also contains one separate unpaired `actual_post` at RIP `0xffffffff81809fa1`, for raw range `0x7ffffffff000..0x0`; the event is explicit and not hidden by a cap. Candidate association is `prefix_candidates`, and the copy destination is inside the two retained candidate pages.

| Observation | Run 0001 | Run 0002 |
|---|---|---|
| Candidate pages | `0x7fffe29fc000`, `0x7fffe29fd000` | `0x7fff9d9d7000`, `0x7fff9d9d8000` |
| `bprm_p` | upper page + `0xfd2` | upper page + `0xfd2` |
| `aligned_stack_pointer` | upper page + `0xa80` | upper page − `0xbd0` (lower page + `0x430`) |
| Copy destination / length | upper page + `0xa79` / 7 bytes | lower page + `0x429` / 7 bytes |
| Setup page walks | both candidates non-present at PD | both candidates non-present at PDPT |
| Initial and return page walks | lower candidate non-present at PT; upper maps to `0x39ff000` | lower candidate non-present at PT; upper maps to `0x39ff000` |
| Delivered fault at copy destination | none | #PF at `0x7fff9d9d7429`, error code `0x2` (write, not-present), original guest-access walk ends non-present at PT |

Both `bprm_p` values are at offset `+0xfd2` in their respective upper candidate pages. The aligned-pointer offsets relative to those pages are `+0xa80` and `-0xbd0`, a normalized offset difference of `0x1650`; equivalently, the `bprm_p`-to-aligned-pointer distances are `0x552` and `0x1ba2`. The same seven-byte copy length is subtracted afterward. The replay localizes the differing copy outcome: run 0001's destination lies in the mapped upper candidate page, while run 0002's destination lies in the absent lower candidate page and matches its additional delivered #PF. The snapshots do not identify why the aligned pointer differs, when the lower mapping first diverged, or whether a particular CR3 write caused it. In run 0002 the lower page is already non-present at the captured initial phase; the trace does not provide continuous page-table history.

## Result and next step

Schema-v20 exact replay integrity is verified for both canonical nonces, and the new capture narrows the differing copy result to the aligned-pointer value and the mapped/unmapped candidate page at the sampled phases. The aggregate `incomplete` status reflects the explicit extra unpaired event; it does not mean the four phases or page-walk records were omitted. This replay does not run or satisfy the strict source-pair comparator, explain the origin of the aligned-pointer difference, establish CR3 causality, or accept S5-07. No comparator or eligibility rule changed.

The diagnostic replay slice is complete. Next integrate local `main` at `1ef4897` as a separate slice, repeat focused checks and measurements on that RAM/MMU backend, then revisit the `aligned_stack_pointer` difference using the paired v20 evidence. Keep S5-07 blocked/unaccepted until its existing strict acceptance gate passes.

